1. SetState is the basic and built-in state management 
method in Flutter. Used for local widget-level state 
Rebuilds the entire widget when state changes
Simple and easy to use > Not suitable for large or complex 
applications Best for: small screens, simple UI updates 
2. ProviderProvider is a wrapper around InheritedWidget
and is widely used. Separates business logic from UIUses
ChangeNotifier and notifyListeners() Improves code 
readability and reusability Easy to learn and maintain
Can become complex for very large apps
Best for: medium-scale applications
3.Riverpod: riverpod is an improved and safer version of 
Provider. > No dependency on BuildContext Compile-time 
safety Better performance and scalability Easy testing 
support Slight learning curve compared to Provider
Best for: scalable and production-level apps
4. GetX :GetX is a lightweight and all-in-one solution. 
Handles state management, navigation, and dependency 
injection Very fast performance Minimal boilerplate code 
Easy to use for beginners Overuse can lead to poor 
architecture if not structured well Best for: rapid 
development and small-to-medium apps